        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4498855c-a1da-5b25-88e7-63ba4f6e4d6e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Clianthus, Clianthus maximus, Callicoma serratifolia\n- Genera: Clianthus, Callicoma\n- Places: New Zealand, Australia\n- Concepts: Fabaceae, flowering plants, shrubs, small trees\n\nFacts:\n- Clianthus is a genus of flowering plants in the legume family Fabaceae.\n- Clianthus is commonly known as kakabeak and as kōwhai ngutukākā in Māori.\n- Clianthus comprises two species of shrubs native to New Zealand.\n- Clianthus maximus is one of the two species in the genus Clianthus.\n- The two Clianthus species have striking clusters of red flowers that resemble the beak of the kākā, a New Zealand parrot.\n- Callicoma is a plant genus that contains one species, Callicoma serratifolia.\n- Callicoma serratifolia is a tall shrub or small tree native to Australia.",
